# AARON curated class-balance additions — MEASURED AND REJECTED in 0.3.
#
# The idea was sound: the hard negatives grew the `unknown` class from
# 163 to 194 and the imbalance from 2.56x to 4.09x, so the other
# thirteen classes were given more data to compensate.
#
# It made every measure worse:
#
#   locked benchmark  accuracy 0.6385  macro-F1 0.6466  false-accept 0.4000
#   regression suite  37/42
#   safety benchmark  refused 0.4510  side-effecting false-accept 0.2353
#
# against the shipped configuration's 0.7308 / 0.7411 / 0.2800, 42/42 and
# 0.4804 / 0.1863. The additions were mostly the same *shape* as existing
# examples — "show me the file X" for a dozen X — so they added volume
# without adding coverage. More rows of the same kind is not more data.
#
# Kept so the experiment can be repeated.
